                  <div class="aalto-article__hub-text">

                    <a href="/en/wood-program" hreflang="en">Wood Program</a>
            </div>
        
                <h1>
  A•LAVA Project Information</h1>
                                          <div class="aalto-article__ingress">
            
                    A•LAVA is a summer theatre built to serve the needs of Annantalo, a Youth Arts Centre in Helsinki. It was created by the Wood Program at Aalto University.
            
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

          <div class="aalto-article__hero-wrap full-bleed-container full-bleed-container--hero">
        <div class="aalto-article__hero-container aalto-article__hero-container--default">
                    


<figure>
  <div class="">
    <div class="media-with-caption__container">
      
                    


  
      
                        <picture>
                  <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/2_3_1040w_452h_n/public/2019-11/main-alava.jpg?h=a8636ecf&amp;itok=Fo0Y-LbO 1040w, /sites/default/files/styles/2_3_1380w_600h_n/public/2019-11/main-alava.jpg?h=a8636ecf&amp;itok=qhYO0KPa 1380w" media="all and (min-width: 992px)" type="image/jpeg" sizes="(min-width: 1540px) 1380px, (min-width: 992px) calc(100vw - 160px), calc(100vw - 160px)" width="1380" height="600"/>
              <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/1_6_567w_354h_n/public/2019-11/main-alava.jpg?h=a8636ecf&amp;itok=v1qsPgXj 567w, /sites/default/files/styles/1_6_819w_512h_n/public/2019-11/main-alava.jpg?h=a8636ecf&amp;itok=dso7vgme 819w" media="all and (max-width: 991px)" type="image/jpeg" sizes="(min-width: 740px) calc(100vw - 80px), (min-width: 320px) calc(100vw - 32px), 288px" width="819" height="512"/>
                  <img loading="eager" width="567" height="354" data-original-width="5984" data-original-height="3366" src="/sites/default/files/styles/1_6_567w_354h_n/public/2019-11/main-alava.jpg?h=a8636ecf&amp;itok=v1qsPgXj" alt="A•LAVA summer theatre under constuction by the Wood Program at Aalto University. Photos: Marc Goodwin &amp; Philip Tidwell" />

  </picture>


            
  

            
    </div>
  </div>
  </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    
    
        
          
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>A•LAVA is a summer theatre built to serve the needs of Annantalo, a Youth Arts Centre in Helsinki. The building serves as a performance and exhibition space in an urban lot in Helsinki. It is based on a square shape plan, with varying triangular openings that shape the walls and open the stage in three directions. The roof follows the same principles, raising up to emphasize the location of the stage.</p>
<p><strong>Completion:</strong><br>June, 2017</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong><br>The summer theatre was constructed for the Annantalo Youth Arts Centre in Helsinki to serve as an open air performance and exhibition space.</p>
<p><strong>Area:</strong><br>65m<sup>2</sup> (roof canopy)<br>124m<sup>2</sup> (deck)</p>
<p><strong>​Architectural Design and Construction:</strong><br>​Mathias Björkman, Alba Esther Aguilar Bustamante, Caio Cintra, Rodrigo Giorgi, Riccardo Guerri, Emilia Almqvist Jansson, Noora Kassinen, Loreto Mancilla, Elsa Mendoza, Guido Mitidieri, Teodor Nilson, Tatsuro Sakata, Andrea Settimi, Heidi Silvennoinen, Hannah Smith, Kire Stavrov, Jianlin Sun, Kenji Takahashi, Paul Texereau, Sonja Äärilä</p>
<p><strong>Structural Design:</strong><br>Antti Haikala (Pentinmikko Engineering)</p>
<p><strong>Instructors:</strong><br>Philip Tidwell, Pekka Heikkinen, Willem van Bolderen</p>
<p><strong>Materials:</strong><br>Walls – dimensional spruce (untreated)<br>Roof Beams – glue laminated spruce<br>Roof Surface – water-treated laminated roof panels (Kerto-kate)<br>Waterproof Roof – PVC coated textile<br>Decking – heat-treated pine</p>
<p><strong>Suppliers:</strong><br>Würth (hardware), Lunawood (Heat-treated decking)</p>
<p><strong>Photos:</strong><br>Marc Goodwin, Philip Tidwell</p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  

